      "protocols_note": "The matrix tracks host-dispatchable protocols (check_dispatch.py KNOWN_PROTOCOLS / dispatch()). Protocols 0x35 (53) and 0x39 (57) ALSO dispatch to configure_flash_5v_page in firmware (memory.cpp) and ARE covered by the Tier-1 native suite test_val_5v_page.cpp (hard-coded make_handle(0x35,...)/make_handle(0x39,...), calling configure_memory directly). However, zero chips in chip_database.json carry algorithm=0x35 or 0x39, so the host dispatch path never routes to configure_flash_5v_page via those protocols. They are intentionally omitted here to keep the host matrix consistent with the host dispatch mirror (CR-02 resolution, 2026-06-16). This is NOT a regression — the firmware truth and native coverage are preserved in test_val_5v_page.cpp.",
